</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Grad-CAM.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">When compared to Grad-CAM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Selvaraju et al., 2016</a>)</cite>, which is often applied in several zero-shot RIS approaches <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Subramanian et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee et al., 2023a</a>)</cite>, Figure <a href="#A3.F17" title="Figure 17 ‣ Appendix C Additional Results ‣ CoPatch: Zero-Shot Referring Image Segmentation by Leveraging Untapped Spatial Knowledge in CLIP" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a> demonstrates that our <span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CoMap</span> can provide better spatial cues for a primary object from a referring expression. Furthermore, our <span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CoPatch</span> (using <span id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">CoMap</span>) takes less inference time than IteRPrimE, which uses Grad-CAM, as shown in Table <a href="#A3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Segmentation Approaches. ‣ C.1 Spatial Map Comparison ‣ Appendix C Additional Results ‣ CoPatch: Zero-Shot Referring Image Segmentation by Leveraging Untapped Spatial Knowledge in CLIP" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> while achieving better IoU performance.</p>
</div>
