<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 9: </span><span id="A3.T9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Performance comparison between attention-based (<span id="A3.T9.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Attn</span>) and weighted-sum-based (<span id="A3.T9.4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">WS</span>) fusion strategies across RefCOCOg, RefCOCO, and RefCOCO+ (10%) validation datasets</span>. We observe that the best performance is achieved using exit layers from the middle layers that are closer to the final layers for both fusion methods.</figcaption>
</figure>
